    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "2.1 Deﬁnition of the model"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 18,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 83.667, 539.0, 512.333, 626.333 ],
    "font" : "CMR12",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Throughout, we use the notation N : = { 1 , 2 , . . . } , N 0 : = N ∪{ 0 } and [ n ] : = { 1 , . . ., n } for each n ∈ N . We consider a labeled directed graph ( V, E ) with vertex set V = [ n ] for some n ∈ N and edge set E ⊂ { ( v, w ): v, w ∈ V } . The natural number representing a vertex is then referred to as its label . In such a graph, a sequence of vertices ( v 1 , v 2 , . . ., v k +1 ) is a directed path of length k ∈ N if"
  }, {
    "type" : "formula",
    "pdfua_tag" : "Formula",
    "id" : 19,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 239.381, 509.207, 354.612, 522.877 ],
    "content" : ""
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 20,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 84.333, 474.333, 314.667, 491.0 ],
    "font" : "CMBX12",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "and an undirected path of length k ∈ N if"
  }, {
    "type" : "formula",
    "pdfua_tag" : "Formula",
    "id" : 21,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 197.24, 443.999, 395.795, 457.308 ],
    "content" : ""
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 22,
