    "bounding box" : [ 95.333, 408.333, 258.667, 424.667 ],
    "font" : "CMR12",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "labeled directed graph is called"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 23,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 112.667, 360.333, 512.667, 392.667 ],
    "font" : "CMR12",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "connected if, for each pair of vertices, there is an undirected path joining those vertices,"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 24,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 112.0, 313.667, 512.0, 346.667 ],
    "font" : "CMR12",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "acyclic if it does not contain any directed cycles, i.e. directed paths that visit the same vertex more than once,"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 25,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 112.333, 284.333, 441.667, 301.333 ],
    "font" : "CMR12",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "increasing if the labels are decreasing along all directed paths."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 26,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 84.0, 160.333, 513.0, 268.333 ],
    "font" : "CMR12",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "We observe that if a graph is increasing, then it is acyclic in particular. For v ∈ V , we call a vertex w ∈ V an out-neighbor if ( v, w ) ∈ E and an in-neighbor if ( w, v ) ∈ E . Then, the number of out-neighbors of v is denoted by outdeg ( v ). On the other hand, we call the number of in-neighbors of v the degree of vertex v , denoted by d V ( v ). For all n, m ∈ N we deﬁne I ( m ) n to be the set of increasing directed graphs on [ n ] satisfying the condition"
  }, {
